                      (        forth.asm):00001         * 6309 Forth based on my 1984/07/16 TRS-80 Model 1 level II ROM implementation.
                      (        forth.asm):00002         *
                      (        forth.asm):00003         * This work is dedicated to Alain Pinaud, author of "Programmer en Forth"
                      (        forth.asm):00004         * published by Editions du P.S.I. in 1983--i.e. my virtual mentor in the field.
                      (        forth.asm):00005         * Special thanks go William Astle for his fantastic LW Tools utility set and
                      (        forth.asm):00006         * to Robert Lipe for his advice on serial line handling. Apache subversion
                      (        forth.asm):00007         * and the sdiff utility also were on my side all the time.
                      (        forth.asm):00008         *
                      (        forth.asm):00009         * Also credited for their help: Justin Poirier (seminal HW design), Daniel
                      (        forth.asm):00010         * Tufvesson (original CompactFlash interface), Peter Minuth (general Forth
                      (        forth.asm):00011         * guruness), Paul E. Bennett (ANSI compatibility advice); Michel Jean, Bill
                      (        forth.asm):00012         * Ragsdale, Pablo Hugo Reda, Matthias Koch, Demitri Peynado and Bernd Paysan
                      (        forth.asm):00013         * for contributed application level code; Carsten Strotmann for most of the
                      (        forth.asm):00014         * benchmarking code (see https://theultimatebenchmark.org/); Gerry Jackson and
                      (        forth.asm):00015         * Steve R. Palmer (see https://github.com/gerryjackson/forth2012-test-suite)
                      (        forth.asm):00016         * for selected bits and pieces of the Forth2012 test suite
                      (        forth.asm):00017         * (see https://forth-standard.org/).
                      (        forth.asm):00018         *
                      (        forth.asm):00019         * This is a native Forth. Not a threaded interpretive implementation.
                      (        forth.asm):00020         * Worth noticing is the fact that the return stack does not hold return
                      (        forth.asm):00021         * addresses at all. All what is stored there is loop indexes and input stream
                      (        forth.asm):00022         * parameters. Actual return addresses are kept in the system stack. All in all,
                      (        forth.asm):00023         * this is the result of the work of a 19 year old, heavily revisited 35 years
                      (        forth.asm):00024         * later. The downside of this implementation is that the generated code is
                      (        forth.asm):00025         * about 30% larger than a threaded interpretive implementation would be.
                      (        forth.asm):00026         * So it goes...
                      (        forth.asm):00027         *
                      (        forth.asm):00028         * Control flow constructs have been re-implemented based on Wonyong Koh's
                      (        forth.asm):00029         * hForth for the 8086. The original code can be consulted at
                      (        forth.asm):00030         * https://github.com/nealcrook/hForth. Of particular interest is
                      (        forth.asm):00031         * 8086/HF86RAM.ASM. Entries on the control flow stack (implemented on the
                      (        forth.asm):00032         * data stack here) are two cell entities that consist of a parameter
                      (        forth.asm):00033         * (an address), on the top of which a tag identifying the type of address
                      (        forth.asm):00034         * is pushed. They are:
                      (        forth.asm):00035         *
                      (        forth.asm):00036         * Control-flow stack item    Representation (parameter and type)
                      (        forth.asm):00037         * -----------------------    -------------------------------------
                      (        forth.asm):00038         * dest                       control-flow destination      0
                      (        forth.asm):00039         * orig                       control-flow origin           1
                      (        forth.asm):00040         * of-sys                     OF origin                     2 [1]
                      (        forth.asm):00041         * case-sys                   x (any value)                 3 [1]
                      (        forth.asm):00042         * do-sys                     ?DO origin                    DO destination
                      (        forth.asm):00043         * colon-sys                  xt of current definition     -1 [1]
                      (        forth.asm):00044         *
                      (        forth.asm):00045         * [1] Not implemented in Z79Forth/A.
                      (        forth.asm):00046         * 
                      (        forth.asm):00047         * This mechanism allows for verification of balanced control flow constructs.
                      (        forth.asm):00048         *
                      (        forth.asm):00049         * The code generated is limited to a very small instruction set:
                      (        forth.asm):00050         *
                      (        forth.asm):00051         * LDXOPC        $8E     LDX (immediate)
                      (        forth.asm):00052         * JMPOPC        $7E     JMP (extended)
                      (        forth.asm):00053         * JSROPC        $BD     JSR (extended)
                      (        forth.asm):00054         * RTSOPC        $39     RTS (inherent)
                      (        forth.asm):00055         * BCSOPC        $2503   BCS *+5 (relative) Used in LOOP, +LOOP
                      (        forth.asm):00056         * BNEOPC        $2603   BNE *+5 (relative) Used in ?DO, IF, UNTIL
                      (        forth.asm):00057         *
                      (        forth.asm):00058         * On error, the system stack pointer is reset. The return stack also is
                      (        forth.asm):00059         * but the data stack will be in the same state as when the error occurred.
                      (        forth.asm):00060         * ABORT and QUIT enforce their own ANS94 standard behaviour.
                      (        forth.asm):00061         *
                      (        forth.asm):00062         * RESTRICT is non-standard. It comes from GNU Forth (VolksForth). The " OK"
                      (        forth.asm):00063         * non-prompt string also does, by the way. Thanks to Anton Ertl for his terse
                      (        forth.asm):00064         * yet valuable input.
                      (        forth.asm):00065         *
                      (        forth.asm):00066         * .' (dot-tick) is non-standard. It comes from SwiftForth. It will be supported
                      (        forth.asm):00067         * whether or not the symbolic stack dump has been configured (see SSDFEAT in
                      (        forth.asm):00068         * constants.asm). However, please note that effective symbolic references will
                      (        forth.asm):00069         * be resolved only if the feature was enabled at compilation time. Otherwise
                      (        forth.asm):00070         * a simple HEX print of the cell at the top of the data stack will be
                      (        forth.asm):00071         * performed. This is meant to support Forth source code that does not depend
                      (        forth.asm):00072         * on the feature vector (see examples/dis.4th).
                      (        forth.asm):00073         *
                      (        forth.asm):00074         * MONITOR and ICHECK are also non-standard. They are intended to maintain and
                      (        forth.asm):00075         * verify the integrity of a checksum of the code section of RAM resident
                      (        forth.asm):00076         * words, with the exception of VARIABLEs and CREATEd words. CREATEd words,
                      (        forth.asm):00077         * if subject to the MONITOR treatment will also carry a code section
                      (        forth.asm):00078         * checksum, although this is not the default behaviour. The checksum will
                      (        forth.asm):00079         * consist in an extra byte added to every word's header. MONITOR and ICHECK
                      (        forth.asm):00080         * will be available whether or not the reliability feature has been configured
                      (        forth.asm):00081         * (see RELFEAT in constants.asm). They will only carry effective semantics
                      (        forth.asm):00082         * if the feature was actually enabled at compilation time. This is meant to
                      (        forth.asm):00083         * support Forth source code that does not depend on the feature vector.
                      (        forth.asm):00084         *
                      (        forth.asm):00085         * Experimental MC146818 RTC support: the feature is disabled by default
                      (        forth.asm):00086         * (see RTCFEAT in constants.asm) because it relies on undocumented schematics.
                      (        forth.asm):00087         * Also, the required underlying circuitry is not intended to ever become an
                      (        forth.asm):00088         * integral part of the Z79Forth reference board itself. Some better designed
                      (        forth.asm):00089         * form of it might eventually surface in the form of an extension specification.
                      (        forth.asm):00090         * At the time of this writing this is just a proof of concept, but whether or
                      (        forth.asm):00091         * not the feature is enabled, three extra words will be added to the dictionary.
                      (        forth.asm):00092         * They are RTC@ RTC! and TICKS They can be safely ignored.
                      (        forth.asm):00093         *
                      (        forth.asm):00094         * Forth source code portability note:
                      (        forth.asm):00095         * Because Z79Forth does not use the return stack to store return addresses,
                      (        forth.asm):00096         * it makes it quite easy to write code that is not readily portable to classic
                      (        forth.asm):00097         * threaded interpretive implementations. The resulting code will be simpler but
                      (        forth.asm):00098         * portability will be limited.
                      (        forth.asm):00099         *
                      (        forth.asm):00100         * Miscellaneous notes: RA stands for return address; EP for entry point.
                      (        forth.asm):00101         * CF is a shortcut for CompactFlash. TOS means top of the data/normal stack.
                      (        forth.asm):00102         * Occasionally, CFA is used for code field address which, in this
                      (        forth.asm):00103         * implementation, is a synonym for compilation address. XT means execution
                      (        forth.asm):00104         * token--the ANSI term for a compilation address. MSC stands for most
                      (        forth.asm):00105         * significant cell; LSC for least significant cell.
                      (        forth.asm):00106         *
                      (        forth.asm):00107         * The complete guide to the HD6309 extended instruction set can be found at:
                      (        forth.asm):00108         * https://cyberabi.ipower.com/Downloads/The_6309_Book.pdf. For convenience,
                      (        forth.asm):00109         * and with the author's explicit agreement, this document has been included
                      (        forth.asm):00110         * in this distribution. This is recommended reading for anyone altering this
                      (        forth.asm):00111         * code or trying to make some sense of it!!!
                      (        forth.asm):00112         *
                      (        forth.asm):00113         * This whole effort started out as a porting endeavour and ended up being a
                      (        forth.asm):00114         * substantial rewrite, trying to take advantage of the features of the 6309
                      (        forth.asm):00115         * as much as possible. The primary goals of this implementation are:
                      (        forth.asm):00116         * reliability, performance and code compactness. A number of bugs in the
                      (        forth.asm):00117         * original code have been fixed--some remain for sure!
                      (        forth.asm):00118         *
                      (        forth.asm):00119         * Obligatory literary reference:
                      (        forth.asm):00120         * "The paper is very heavy going, and I should never have read it, had I not
                      (        forth.asm):00121         * written it myself." John E. Littlewood (1885-1977).
                      (        forth.asm):00122         *
                      (        forth.asm):00123         * The original soundtrack for this work is available at:
                      (        forth.asm):00124         * https://youtu.be/YqXZtGyFyDo?t=4023 (J.S. Bach BWV 1080, contrapunctus 14).
                      (        forth.asm):00125         
0000                  (        forth.asm):00126         pragma  opt cd,operandsizewarning
                      (        forth.asm):00127         
                      (        forth.asm):00128                 include constants.asm
                      (    constants.asm):00001         * Begin tunable parameters section.
                      (    constants.asm):00002         
     0000             (    constants.asm):00003         CSSNTVE equ     0               Words and HEX numbers are case sensitive if NZ
     0000             (    constants.asm):00004         SSDFEAT equ     0               Set to 1 to enable the symbolic stack dump feat.
     0001             (    constants.asm):00005         RELFEAT set     1               Set to 1 to enable the reliability feature
                      (    constants.asm):00006         
     0001             (    constants.asm):00007         WTCFEAT equ     1               MECB SYS I/O RTC
     0000             (    constants.asm):00008         RTCFEAT equ     0               Cool but the reliability feature must go...
     0000             (    constants.asm):00009         DEBUG   set     0               Enforce assertions and miscellaneous checks
     0001             (    constants.asm):00010         HVNMI   equ     1               NMI handler support
     0000             (    constants.asm):00011         HVNMI2  equ     0               NMI handler support (async input debugging)
                      (    constants.asm):00012         * Loop count for MS. This is busy waiting, so we depend on the CPU clock speed.
     00C2             (    constants.asm):00013         MSLCNT  equ     194             at 1 MHz native mode (MECB)
                      (    constants.asm):00014         *MSLCNT equ     794             at 4 MHz native mode
                      (    constants.asm):00015         *MSLCNT equ     994             at 5 MHz native mode
                      (    constants.asm):00016         
                      (    constants.asm):00017         * End tunable parameters section.
                      (    constants.asm):00018         
                      (    constants.asm):00019                 IFNE    RTCFEAT
0000                  (    constants.asm):00020         RELFEAT set     0               RTCFEAT disables RELFEAT
                      (    constants.asm):00021                 ELSE
                      (    constants.asm):00022                 IFNE    HVNMI
                      (    constants.asm):00023                 IFNE    HVNMI2
0000                  (    constants.asm):00024         RELFEAT set     0               (HVNMI and HVNMI2) disable RELFEAT
                      (    constants.asm):00025                 ENDC                    HVNMI2
                      (    constants.asm):00026                 ENDC                    HVNMI
                      (    constants.asm):00027                 ENDC                    RTCFEAT
                      (    constants.asm):00028         
                      (    constants.asm):00029         * Intrinsic ANS94 support prevents both DEBUG and the reliability feature.
     0000             (    constants.asm):00030         RELFEAT set     0
     0000             (    constants.asm):00031         DEBUG   set     0
                      (    constants.asm):00032         
                      (    constants.asm):00033         * Control flow stack implemented on the top of the data stack.
     E659             (    constants.asm):00034         CSPUSH  EQU     NPUSH
     E667             (    constants.asm):00035         CSPOP   EQU     NPOP
                      (    constants.asm):00036         
                      (    constants.asm):00037         * Memory map.
     0000             (    constants.asm):00038         RAMSTRT equ     $0000
     8000             (    constants.asm):00039         RAMSIZE equ     $8000
     C000             (    constants.asm):00040         IOSTRT  equ     $C000
     E000             (    constants.asm):00041         ROMSTRT equ     $E000
     FFF0             (    constants.asm):00042         VECTBL  equ     $FFF0
                      (    constants.asm):00043         
                      (    constants.asm):00044         * Base address for global variables (direct page addressed).
     0100             (    constants.asm):00045         VARSPC  equ     $100
                      (    constants.asm):00046         
                      (    constants.asm):00047         * The 74HCT138 (U7) IO address decoder maps one 1 KB area per usable device.
     C0C0             (    constants.asm):00048         DEV0    equ     $C0C0           Compact Flash memory module (optional)
     C400             (    constants.asm):00049         DEV1    equ     $C400
     C800             (    constants.asm):00050         DEV2    equ     $C800
     CC00             (    constants.asm):00051         DEV3    equ     $CC00
     C040             (    constants.asm):00052         DEV4    equ     $C040       RTC-72421 (optional MECB)
     D400             (    constants.asm):00053         DEV5    equ     $D400           MC146818 RTC (optional)
     C008             (    constants.asm):00054         DEV6    equ     $C008           HD63B50 unit 0
     DC00             (    constants.asm):00055         DEV7    equ     $DC00
                      (    constants.asm):00056         
     C008             (    constants.asm):00057         ACIACTL equ     DEV6
     C009             (    constants.asm):00058         ACIADAT equ     DEV6+1
                      (    constants.asm):00059         
                      (    constants.asm):00060         * ACIA control register bits.
     0003             (    constants.asm):00061         ACRST   equ     %00000011       ACIA master reset
                      (    constants.asm):00062         
                      (    constants.asm):00063         * 1.84320 MHz Y1: 115200 bps in the direct path, 38400 bps in the DIV3 path
     0001             (    constants.asm):00064         ACDIV16 equ     %00000001       ACIA div 16
                      (    constants.asm):00065         
     0014             (    constants.asm):00066         AC8N1   equ     %00010100       ACIA 8N1
     0000             (    constants.asm):00067         ACRTS0  equ     %00000000       ACIA RTS# low
     0040             (    constants.asm):00068         ACRTS1  equ     %01000000       ACIA RTS# high
     0080             (    constants.asm):00069         ACRDINT equ     %10000000       IRQ on RDRF
                      (    constants.asm):00070         
     0043             (    constants.asm):00071         ACIRSET equ     ACRTS1|ACRST
     00D5             (    constants.asm):00072         ACIRTS1 equ     ACRTS1|ACRDINT|AC8N1|ACDIV16
     0095             (    constants.asm):00073         ACIRTS0 equ     ACRTS0|ACRDINT|AC8N1|ACDIV16
                      (    constants.asm):00074         
                      (    constants.asm):00075         * ACIA status register bits.
     0001             (    constants.asm):00076         ACIRDRF equ     %00000001       Receive data register full
     0002             (    constants.asm):00077         ACITDRE equ     %00000010       Transmit data register empty
     0020             (    constants.asm):00078         ACIOVRN equ     %00100000       Overrun status register bit
     0080             (    constants.asm):00079         ACIISVC equ     %10000000       Interrupt needs servicing
                      (    constants.asm):00080         
                      (    constants.asm):00081         * Compact Flash parameters.
     C0C0             (    constants.asm):00082         CFBASE  equ     DEV0
     C0C0             (    constants.asm):00083         CFDATAR equ     CFBASE          R/W data register
     C0C1             (    constants.asm):00084         CFERROR equ     CFBASE+1        RO error register
     C0C1             (    constants.asm):00085         CFFEATR equ     CFBASE+1        WO features register
     C0C2             (    constants.asm):00086         CFSCNTR equ     CFBASE+2        R/W sector count register
     C0C3             (    constants.asm):00087         CFSNUMR equ     CFBASE+3        R/W sector number register
     C0C4             (    constants.asm):00088         CFCLOWR equ     CFBASE+4        R/W cylinder low register
     C0C5             (    constants.asm):00089         CFCHIGR equ     CFBASE+5        R/W cylinder high register
     C0C6             (    constants.asm):00090         CFDRHDR equ     CFBASE+6        R/W drive/head register
     C0C7             (    constants.asm):00091         CFSTATR equ     CFBASE+7        RO status register
     C0C7             (    constants.asm):00092         CFCOMDR equ     CFBASE+7        WO command register
                      (    constants.asm):00093         
                      (    constants.asm):00094         * CF status bits.
     0080             (    constants.asm):00095         CFBSYB  equ     %10000000       BSY status bit
     0040             (    constants.asm):00096         CFRDYB  equ     %01000000       RDY status bit
     0020             (    constants.asm):00097         CFDWFB  equ     %00100000       DWF status bit (not used)
     0010             (    constants.asm):00098         CFDSCB  equ     %00010000       DSC status bit (not used)
     0008             (    constants.asm):00099         CFDRQB  equ     %00001000       DRQ status bit
     0001             (    constants.asm):00100         CFERRB  equ     %00000001       ERR status bit
                      (    constants.asm):00101         
     0200             (    constants.asm):00102         CFSCSZ  equ     $200            Compact Flash (IDE) sector size
                      (    constants.asm):00103         
                      (    constants.asm):00104         * CF commands.
     00EC             (    constants.asm):00105         CFIDDEV equ     $EC             Identify Device
     00EF             (    constants.asm):00106         CFSETFT equ     $EF             Set Feature
     0020             (    constants.asm):00107         CFRSCTS equ     $20             Read Sectors
     0030             (    constants.asm):00108         CFWSCTS equ     $30             Write Sectors
                      (    constants.asm):00109         
                      (    constants.asm):00110         * Buffer in-memory structure:
                      (    constants.asm):00111         * data: 1024 bytes.
                      (    constants.asm):00112         * terminator: 1 byte set to 0.
                      (    constants.asm):00113         * flags: 1 byte.
                      (    constants.asm):00114         * blknum: 2 bytes.
     0001             (    constants.asm):00115         BINUSE  equ     1               Buffer is allocated (the blknum field is valid)
     0002             (    constants.asm):00116         BMAPPD  equ     2               Block has been read from the CF device
     0004             (    constants.asm):00117         BDIRTY  equ     4               Block has been marked for update
     0400             (    constants.asm):00118         BLKSIZ  equ     2*CFSCSZ        Block size is 2 CF sectors (1 KB)
                      (    constants.asm):00119         * Buffer field offsets.
     0400             (    constants.asm):00120         BOTERM  equ     BLKSIZ          Base buffer to the 'terminator' field offset
     0401             (    constants.asm):00121         BOFLAGS equ     BLKSIZ+1        Base buffer to the 'flag' field offset
     0402             (    constants.asm):00122         BOBLKNO equ     BLKSIZ+2        Base buffer to the 'blknum' field offset
                      (    constants.asm):00123         
     0410             (    constants.asm):00124         BFDISP  equ     BUF1-BUF0       Offset between resident buffers
                      (    constants.asm):00125         
                      (    constants.asm):00126         ;;;
                      (    constants.asm):00127         ;;; RTC-72421 registers
                      (    constants.asm):00128         ;;; 
     C040             (    constants.asm):00129         rtc_base        equ     DEV4
     C040             (    constants.asm):00130         rtc_reg_s1      equ     rtc_base+$0     ; 1-second digit
     C041             (    constants.asm):00131         rtc_reg_s10     equ     rtc_base+$1     ; 10-seconds digit
     C042             (    constants.asm):00132         rtc_reg_mi1     equ     rtc_base+$2     ; 1-minute digit
     C043             (    constants.asm):00133         rtc_reg_mi10    equ     rtc_base+$3     ; 10-minutes digit
     C044             (    constants.asm):00134         rtc_reg_h1      equ     rtc_base+$4     ; 1-hour digit
     C045             (    constants.asm):00135         rtc_reg_h10     equ     rtc_base+$5     ; 10-hours digit
     C046             (    constants.asm):00136         rtc_reg_d1      equ     rtc_base+$6     ; 1-day digit
     C047             (    constants.asm):00137         rtc_reg_d10     equ     rtc_base+$7     ; 10-days digit
     C048             (    constants.asm):00138         rtc_reg_mo1     equ     rtc_base+$8     ; 1-month digit
     C049             (    constants.asm):00139         rtc_reg_mo10    equ     rtc_base+$9     ; 10-months digit
     C04A             (    constants.asm):00140         rtc_reg_y1      equ     rtc_base+$a     ; 1-year digit
     C04B             (    constants.asm):00141         rtc_reg_y10     equ     rtc_base+$b     ; 10-years digit
     C04C             (    constants.asm):00142         rtc_reg_w       equ     rtc_base+$c     ; Day of week
     C04D             (    constants.asm):00143         rtc_reg_cd      equ     rtc_base+$d     ; Control reg D
     C04E             (    constants.asm):00144         rtc_reg_ce      equ     rtc_base+$e     ; Control reg E
     C04F             (    constants.asm):00145         rtc_reg_cf      equ     rtc_base+$f     ; Control reg F
                      (    constants.asm):00146         
                      (    constants.asm):00147         
                      (    constants.asm):00148         * MC146818 RTC registers.
     D400             (    constants.asm):00149         RTAS    equ     DEV5            Latch target register address offset
     D401             (    constants.asm):00150         RTDS    equ     (DEV5+1)        Actual target register access
                      (    constants.asm):00151         * RTC internal register offsets.
     0000             (    constants.asm):00152         RTOSEC  equ     0               Seconds
     0001             (    constants.asm):00153         RTOSECA equ     1               Seconds alarm
     0002             (    constants.asm):00154         RTOMIN  equ     2               Minutes
     0003             (    constants.asm):00155         RTOMINA equ     3               Minutes alarm
     0004             (    constants.asm):00156         RTOHOUR equ     4               Hours
     0005             (    constants.asm):00157         RTOHRA  equ     5               Hours alarm
     0006             (    constants.asm):00158         RTODOW  equ     6               Day of week
     0007             (    constants.asm):00159         RTODOM  equ     7               Day of month
     0008             (    constants.asm):00160         RTOMON  equ     8               Month
     0009             (    constants.asm):00161         RTOYEAR equ     9               Year
     000A             (    constants.asm):00162         RTOREGA equ     10              Register A
     000B             (    constants.asm):00163         RTOREGB equ     11              Register B
     000C             (    constants.asm):00164         RTOREGC equ     12              Register C
     000D             (    constants.asm):00165         RTOREGD equ     13              Register D
     000E             (    constants.asm):00166         RTOUMB  equ     14              Base of user defined NVRAM storage
     0032             (    constants.asm):00167         RTUMSZ  equ     50              Size of user defined NVRAM storage
     003F             (    constants.asm):00168         RTOPRES equ     (RTOUMB+RTUMSZ-1) RTC NVRAM offset for dectecting dev presence
                      (    constants.asm):00169         
                      (    constants.asm):00170         * Register A bits.
     0080             (    constants.asm):00171         RTAUIP  equ     $80             Update in progress
     0070             (    constants.asm):00172         RTADVRS equ     $70             Divider reset, not in operation
     0020             (    constants.asm):00173         RTADV32 equ     $20             In operation, 32 KHz time base
     000A             (    constants.asm):00174         RTARS64 equ     $A              32 KHz time base, 64 Hz PI (every 15.625 ms)
                      (    constants.asm):00175         
                      (    constants.asm):00176         * Register B bits.
     0080             (    constants.asm):00177         RTBSET  equ     $80
     0040             (    constants.asm):00178         RTBPIE  equ     $40
     0004             (    constants.asm):00179         RTBDM   equ     4               Set to 1 for binary register contents
     0002             (    constants.asm):00180         RTB24   equ     2               Set to 1 for 24 hour format
                      (    constants.asm):00181         
                      (    constants.asm):00182         * Register C bits.
     0040             (    constants.asm):00183         RTCPF   equ     $40             Periodic interrupt pending flag
                      (    constants.asm):00184         
                      (    constants.asm):00185         * ASCII trivia.
     0000             (    constants.asm):00186         NUL     equ     0               End of string marker
     0003             (    constants.asm):00187         ETX     equ     3               Control-C (intr)
     0008             (    constants.asm):00188         BS      equ     8               Backspace
     0009             (    constants.asm):00189         HT      equ     9               Horizontal tab
     000A             (    constants.asm):00190         LF      equ     $0A             Aka new line
     000D             (    constants.asm):00191         CR      equ     $0D             Carriage return
     0015             (    constants.asm):00192         NAK     equ     $15             Control-U (kill)
     0020             (    constants.asm):00193         SP      equ     $20             Aka BL in Forth
     0013             (    constants.asm):00194         XOFF    equ     $13             Aka DC3
     0011             (    constants.asm):00195         XON     equ     $11             Aka DC1
                      (    constants.asm):00196         
                      (    constants.asm):00197         * Stack sizes.
     0100             (    constants.asm):00198         NSTKSZ  equ     256             Expressed in bytes. Now only limited by RAM size
     00FE             (    constants.asm):00199         RSTKSZ  equ     254             Expressed in bytes. Up to 127 nested loops
                      (    constants.asm):00200         
                      (    constants.asm):00201         * Buffer sizes.
     0084             (    constants.asm):00202         CMDBFSZ equ     132             Command line entry buffer
     0050             (    constants.asm):00203         HEXBFSZ equ     80
     0048             (    constants.asm):00204         TBUFSZ  equ     72              Used by VLIST to print word name and CVNSTR
     0054             (    constants.asm):00205         PADBSZ  equ     84              79-STANDARD mandates a minimum of 64 bytes
     0040             (    constants.asm):00206         SERBSZ  equ     64              Serial buffer size. Needs to be a power of 2
                      (    constants.asm):00207         
                      (    constants.asm):00208         * Dictionary flag masks.
     0080             (    constants.asm):00209         IMDFLM  equ     $80             Immediate flag mask
     0040             (    constants.asm):00210         DEFFLM  equ     $40             Compilation only flag mask
                      (    constants.asm):00211                 IFNE    RELFEAT
0000                  (    constants.asm):00212         MONFLM  equ     $20             Monitored flag mask. This indicates that the
                      (    constants.asm):00213         *                               word to which it relates might be checked for
                      (    constants.asm):00214         *                               integrity. This applies by default to all words
                      (    constants.asm):00215         *                               defined with : and all constants. It might
                      (    constants.asm):00216         *                               also apply to any other CREATEd object by
                      (    constants.asm):00217         *                               resorting to the MONITOR word. Using MONITOR
                      (    constants.asm):00218         *                               on variable word contents is guaranteed to
                      (    constants.asm):00219         *                               raise ICHECK's attention.
                      (    constants.asm):00220                 ENDC
                      (    constants.asm):00221         
                      (    constants.asm):00222         * Division function codes and options.
     0000             (    constants.asm):00223         DVFSLMD equ     0               Function is /MOD
     0001             (    constants.asm):00224         DVFMOD  equ     1               Function is MOD
     0002             (    constants.asm):00225         DVFDIV  equ     2               Function is /
     0008             (    constants.asm):00226         DVOA1D  equ     8               Argument 1 is a double (FM/MOD SM/REM)
     0010             (    constants.asm):00227         DVOWSYM equ     16              Want symmetric division (default is floored)
     0007             (    constants.asm):00228         DVFMASK equ     7               Mask for extracting function codes
                      (    constants.asm):00229         
     001F             (    constants.asm):00230         WRLNMSK equ     $1F             31 character is the maximum word length
                      (    constants.asm):00231         
                      (    constants.asm):00232         * 6309 opcodes.
     008E             (    constants.asm):00233         LDXOPC  equ     $8E             LDX (immediate)
     007E             (    constants.asm):00234         JMPOPC  equ     $7E             JMP (extended)
     00BD             (    constants.asm):00235         JSROPC  equ     $BD             JSR (extended)
     0039             (    constants.asm):00236         RTSOPC  equ     $39             RTS (inherent)
     2503             (    constants.asm):00237         BCSOPC  equ     $2503           BCS *+5 (relative)
     2603             (    constants.asm):00238         BNEOPC  equ     $2603           BNE *+5 (relative)
     00C7             (    constants.asm):00239         ILLOPC  equ     $C7             An illegal operation code. Meant to raise a trap
                      (    constants.asm):00240         
     0001             (    constants.asm):00241         CFLAG   equ     1               CC bit 0 (C)
     0004             (    constants.asm):00242         ZFLAG   equ     4               CC bit 2 (Z)
     0010             (    constants.asm):00243         IFLAG   equ     $10             CC bit 4 (I)
     0040             (    constants.asm):00244         FFLAG   equ     $40             CC bit 6 (F)
                      (    constants.asm):00245         
                      (    constants.asm):00246         * RAM based execution token for @.
     0D84             (    constants.asm):00247         RAMFTCH set     WDICSPC+4       Dictionary header overhead is word's length + 3
                      (    constants.asm):00248                 IFNE    RELFEAT         The reliability features adds one byte to the
0000                  (    constants.asm):00249         RAMFTCH set     WDICSPC+5       header: a checksum.
                      (    constants.asm):00250                 ENDC
                      (    constants.asm):00251         
                      (        forth.asm):00129         
                      (        forth.asm):00130         * Unchecked NPUSH. This is for situations in which there is absolutely no
                      (        forth.asm):00131         * chance of overflow. For instance, in case we just popped 2 cells and push
                      (        forth.asm):00132         * back one or two.
0000                  (        forth.asm):00133         UCNPUSH MACRO   NOEXPAND
                      (        forth.asm):00134                 pshu    x
                      (        forth.asm):00135                 ENDM
                      (        forth.asm):00136         
                      (        forth.asm):00137         * Unchecked NPOP. To be used only after trusted words have been invoked, i.e.
                      (        forth.asm):00138         * when one is positively sure that the data stack contains at least one cell.
0000                  (        forth.asm):00139         UCNPOP  MACRO   NOEXPAND
                      (        forth.asm):00140                 pulu    x
                      (        forth.asm):00141                 ENDM
                      (        forth.asm):00142         
                      (        forth.asm):00143         * Make sure minimum data stack requirements are satisfied upon word entry.
                      (        forth.asm):00144         * The requirement is expressed in cell size--2 bytes on the 6309.
                      (        forth.asm):00145         * \1 specifies the required number of cells.
0000                  (        forth.asm):00146         MINDREQ MACRO   NOEXPAND
                      (        forth.asm):00147                 ldd     #NSTBOT-(\1*2)  Cell count one expects to be stacked up
                      (        forth.asm):00148                 bra     CHKNDPT         No return if the condition is not met
                      (        forth.asm):00149                 ENDM
                      (        forth.asm):00150         
                      (        forth.asm):00151         * Reliability feature support: execution tokens.
                      (        forth.asm):00152         * \1 has the opcode we want to emit.
                      (        forth.asm):00153         * \2 has the execution token address, as if the header overhead always
                      (        forth.asm):00154         * was 3 bytes.
0000                  (        forth.asm):00155         RFXT    MACRO   NOEXPAND
                      (        forth.asm):00156                 IFNE    RELFEAT
                      (        forth.asm):00157                 \1      \2+1
                      (        forth.asm):00158                 ELSE
                      (        forth.asm):00159                 \1      \2
                      (        forth.asm):00160                 ENDC                    RELFEAT
                      (        forth.asm):00161                 ENDM
                      (        forth.asm):00162         
                      (        forth.asm):00163         * Reliability feature support: variable word header contents.
                      (        forth.asm):00164         * This is a dummy checksum only used for EEPROM resident words.
                      (        forth.asm):00165         * Those never are checked for code integrity by MONITOR.
0000                  (        forth.asm):00166         RFCS    MACRO   NOEXPAND
                      (        forth.asm):00167                 IFNE    RELFEAT
                      (        forth.asm):00168                 fcb     ILLOPC          Illegal opcode
                      (        forth.asm):00169                 ENDC                    RELFEAT
                      (        forth.asm):00170                 ENDM
                      (        forth.asm):00171         
                      (        forth.asm):00172         *******************************************************************************
